  "response": "{\"thought\": \"The user wants me to act as a story model for a space game called SpaceGame. I need to create a campaign story bible in JSON format based on specific constraints.\",\n\"campaign_title\": \"Echoes of the Void\",\n\"campaign_subtitle\": \"Silence in the Zenith Sector\",\n\"campaign_logline\": \"A scavenger's haul leads to a ghost signal that shouldn't exist.\",\n\"campaign_pitch\": \"You are a freelance pilot operating on the fringes of the Zenith-Aurelia-Vanguard triangle. After recovering a corrupted data core from a derelict freighter, you find yourself caught between corporate interests and a hauntingly rhythmic signal originating from deep within the gate networks. You aren't a hero; you're just someone who wants to stay solvent in a sector where secrets are more valuable than ore.\",\n\"campaign_story_summary\": \"The campaign begins with the player navigating the unstable trade routes between Zenith mining outposts and Aurelia research stations, while Vanguard patrols ensure order. The discovery of a 'Ghost Signal'\u2014a recurring pulse that disrupts navigation systems\u2014creates friction between the three factions. While Zenith wants to weaponize the signal's frequency, Aurelia seeks its origin, and Vanguard aims to silence it for safety. As the player fulfills contracts for all three, they notice commonalities in the locations where the signals are strongest. The ultimate goal is to determine if the signal is a remnant of old infrastructure or something that started responding to human presence.\",\n\"tone\": \"PG-13 frontier space opera with dry, slightly dark humor\",\n\"opening_status_quo\": \"The player is a broke pilot in the Zenith sector, barely keeping their ship running while fulfilling menial delivery and salvage contracts.\",\n\"visible_crisis\": \"Increasing pirate activity (Reavers) and signal interference are making trade routes between Zenith and Aurelia hazardous.\",\n\"hidden_crisis\": \"The 'Ghost Signal' is actually an automated maintenance cycle of a pre-collapse gate network that is beginning to reactivate due to current mining activities.\",\n\"why_now\": \"Recent heavy mining in the Zenith sector has breached a dormant sub-layer, causing the signal's frequency to spike and alert both friendly and hostile entities.\",\n\"player_role\": \"Independent pilot with no official ties, valued for their ability to move between faction zones without raising alarms.\",\n\"kaelen_public_role\": \"Broker, fixer, and contract handler for independent pilots.\",\n\"kaelen_secret_angle\": \"Kaelen has been tracking the 'Ghost Signal' since its first recorded spike three years ago; she knows it is linked to old gate tech but keeps her distance from the official investigations.\",\n\"main_mystery_question\": \"What is the origin and purpose of the Ghost Signal?\",\n\"main_mystery_false_answer\": \"It is a distress signal from a lost colony ship seeking rescue.\",\n\"main_mystery_true_answer_hint\": \"The signal is an automated diagnostic for a gate-stabilization network that senses human activity as a 'system error'.\",\n\"long_term_reveal_direction\": \"The system isn't broken; it's just waiting for someone to provide the correct input or bypass.\",\n\"act_1_name\": \"Static in the Wire\",\n\"act_1_goal\": \"Recover three data fragments from derelict sites and deliver them to Kaelen to establish a reputation.\",\n\"act_1_opening_incident\": \"The player finds an encrypted packet of data on a drifting freighter that contains coordinates for several 'anomalous' locations in the system.\",\n\"act_1_midpoint_turn\": \"A Vanguard patrol intercepts the player, but Kaelen manages to swap the cargo for a 'non-suspicious' delivery at the last second.\",\n\"act_1_finale\": \"The player successfully delivers the final fragment and realizes that all three factions are tracking the same set of coordinates.\",\n\"act_1_player_takeaway\": \"The player learns that the signal is not just noise; it's a specific, recurring pattern that both corporations and militants are desperate to control.\",\n\"starter_mission_title\": \"Scrap and Salvage\",\n\"starter_mission_reason\": \"A local trader lost cargo to a Reaver raid; the player must retrieve it from the wreckage to prove their reliability to Kaelen.\",\n\"starter_enemy_identity\": \"Reaver Scout Ship (Mark IV)\",\n\"starter_enemy_knows\": \"The enemy ship's log contains a single repeated phrase: 'The pulse is getting louder.'\",\n\"starter_mission_aftershock\": \"Kaelen notes that the Reaver crew seemed unusually frantic before their ship was destroyed.\",\n\"zenith_current_problem\": \"Declining ore yields from standard mining sites are forcing them to push deeper into unstable zones.\",\n\"aurelia_current_problem\": \"Their research is being hampered by 'ghost' interference in their long-range communication arrays.\",\n\"vanguard_current_problem\": \"They are struggling to contain the pirate presence and keep trade routes safe from erratic signal behavior.\",\n\"faction_conflict_triangle\": \"Zenith wants the ore; Aurelia wants the data; Vanguard wants the safety. They are constantly trading concessions while ignoring the common source of the issue.\",\n\"neutral_space_pressure\": \"The 'Ghost Signal' causes unpredictable atmospheric fluctuations and localized gravity shifts in neutral zones, making navigation hazardous.\",\n\"recurring_clue_name\": \"The Pulse\",\n\"recurring_clue_signal\": \"A rhythmic 3-second pulse of static that occurs every time the player approaches a gate or an old ruin.\",\n\"recurring_clue_first_appearance\": \"In the starter mission's wreckage, as part of a corrupted log file.\",\n\"recurring_clue_escalation\": \"The frequency and volume of the signal increase as the player travels closer to known 'anomalous' sites.\",\n\"recurring_clue_payoff_hint\": \"Eventually, the pulse perfectly aligns with the gate activation sequence.\",\n\"rumor_trail_name\": \"The Ghost Signal Mystery\",\n\"rumor_trail_id\": \"rumor_trail.ghost_signal_mystery\",\n\"rumor_hint_theme\": \"Stories of a signal that speaks to those who hear it.\",\n\"rumor_clue_templates\": [\n    \"I heard some pilots say the signal is actually a countdown.\",\n    \"The old logs talk about 'Project Echo' before the silence.\"\n],\n\"rumor_discovery_type\": \"hidden_discovery\",\n\"rumor_rarity\": \"uncommon\",\n\"rumor_payoff\": \"Unlocks access to an older, more advanced navigation module for gate travel.\",\n\"gate_horizon_tease\": \"The signal seems to be getting stronger as you approach the next jump point.\",\n\"new_system_reveal_rule\": \"Each new system revealed through a gate will feature a unique environmental hazard related to 'signal interference'.\",\n\"future_faction_te",
